  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present simple: negative with don't/doesn't",
      "title_form": "Negación con don't y doesn't",
      "title_target": "Negation with don't and doesn't",
      "description_md_form": "Para decir que **no** haces algo, usa **don't** (do + not) con *I, you, we, they*. Para *he, she, it*, usa **doesn't** (does + not).\n\n**Estructura:**\n\n- **I/You/We/They + don't + verbo** → *I don't like coffee.*\n- **He/She/It + doesn't + verbo** → *She doesn't know my name.*\n\n**Importante:** con *doesn't*, el verbo va en forma base (sin -s). No digas *She doesn't knows*.\n\nUsa estos verbos: *like, love, hate, want, need, know, think, understand, enjoy*.",
      "description_md_target": "To say you **don't** do something, use **don't** (do + not) with *I, you, we, they*. For *he, she, it*, use **doesn't** (does + not).\n\n**Structure:**\n\n- **I/You/We/They + don't + verb** → *I don't like coffee.*\n- **He/She/It + doesn't + verb** → *She doesn't know my name.*\n\n**Important:** with *doesn't*, the verb is in base form (no -s). Don't say *She doesn't knows*.\n\nUse these verbs: *like, love, hate, want, need, know, think, understand, enjoy*.",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + don't/doesn't + base verb + complement",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "present_simple_negative",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Negación",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
